1
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:17,584
We're with two larger-than-life guests,
Joo Sang-uk and Chae Jung-an.

2
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:20,920
If we reach 6.5% in viewership,
we'll get to go on a trip as a team.

3
00:00:20,987 --> 00:00:22,622
Jung-an, will you also make a pledge?

4
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:24,157
-How about 6.5%?
-It's 6.5%.

5
00:00:24,224 --> 00:00:26,726
-I can do three days.
-Three days.

6
00:00:26,793 --> 00:00:28,161
You're coming too.

7
00:00:29,062 --> 00:00:31,064
-Me?
-Sang-uk's coming too.

8
00:00:31,798 --> 00:00:33,099
Let's go.

9
00:00:33,166 --> 00:00:34,267
Please stay tuned.

10
00:00:34,334 --> 00:00:36,703
Yes, please do. Actually, Jung-an

11
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:39,406
has a reputation
as the nation's ex-girlfriend.

12
00:00:39,472 --> 00:00:43,910
-The drama aired back in 2007.
-In 2007?

13
00:00:43,977 --> 00:00:46,012
-Twenty years ago?
-But people bring it up

14
00:00:46,079 --> 00:00:48,248
every summer, still to this day.

15
00:00:48,314 --> 00:00:51,051
Especially this year,
"Han Yu-ju core" was the trend.

16
00:00:51,117 --> 00:00:53,686
-"Core" is a Gen MZ word, right?
-Yes.

17
00:00:53,753 --> 00:00:58,058
It's a word used to express
a specific aesthetic or vibe.

18
00:00:58,124 --> 00:00:59,759
It's often used by Gen MZ,

19
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:01,761
so please remember that, Hyun-suk.

20
00:01:01,828 --> 00:01:04,397
If we start using it,
it'll be the end of another fad.

21
00:01:04,464 --> 00:01:06,633
-It'll die.
-It's another funeral.

22
00:01:06,699 --> 00:01:09,069
-We're a funeral home company.
-If we used the word "core,"

23
00:01:09,135 --> 00:01:11,438
-I'd ask, "Do you have weak core muscles?"
-Exactly.

24
00:01:11,504 --> 00:01:14,207
-"Engage your core."
-It's important.

25
00:01:14,674 --> 00:01:16,509
MEANWHILE…

26
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:18,344
-"Engage your core."
-It's important.

27
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:20,880
-What's she doing?
-Wait a second.

28
00:01:20,947 --> 00:01:24,250
-Chef Eun-yeong.
-She has a new hairstyle.

29
00:01:24,317 --> 00:01:26,820
You've been on my nerves
since the last episode, but I kept quiet.

30
00:01:26,886 --> 00:01:28,555
PUT UP WITH THE EYESORE(?)

31
00:01:28,621 --> 00:01:32,058
-Her eyes look strange too.
-I thought maybe you had a problem.

32
00:01:32,125 --> 00:01:34,961
-But what are you doing?
-Her hair looks different too.

33
00:01:35,028 --> 00:01:39,099
I've been in my Han Yu-ju core era

34
00:01:39,165 --> 00:01:43,970
-for about a decade now.
-She kept staying in that era?

35
00:01:44,037 --> 00:01:47,207
-Do you need to let your hair down?
-To get into Han Yu-ju core,

36
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:48,975
you should part your hair
in 7:3 or 8:2 ratio.

37
00:01:50,076 --> 00:01:53,546
Like this.
You have to cover one side like this.

38
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:55,248
-This is it.
-Why is your neck tilted?

39
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:56,850
-I have to do that.
-What's wrong?

40
00:01:56,916 --> 00:01:58,751
-Is your head too heavy?
-Yu-ju has

41
00:01:58,818 --> 00:02:00,487
-to look a bit tragic.
-Isn't that a ghost?

42
00:02:00,553 --> 00:02:02,822
-Also, melancholic eyes.
-Without these bright lights,

43
00:02:02,889 --> 00:02:06,493
-you'd turn us into a ghost story show.
-You look like a water ghost.

44
00:02:06,559 --> 00:02:08,294
-Like <i>Woman's Wail.</i>
-Those eyes are melancholic?

45
00:02:08,361 --> 00:02:10,864
-Yes, like an ex-girlfriend.
-Not a lunatic?

46
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:12,499
A woman you can't forget.

47
00:02:12,565 --> 00:02:14,567
-What? An ex-girlfriend.
-An ex-girlfriend.

48
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:16,169
That's so scary.

49
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:17,437
-I see.
-My gosh.

50
00:02:17,504 --> 00:02:19,806
Can you breathe a little?

51
00:02:20,173 --> 00:02:21,407
PERFECT LIGHT

52
00:02:21,741 --> 00:02:24,277
IT'S ME… YOUR EX-GIRLFRIEND…

53
00:02:24,344 --> 00:02:26,179
She reminds me of <i>Woman's Wail.</i>

54
00:02:26,246 --> 00:02:29,215
We should turn her shot
into black-and-white.

55
00:02:29,516 --> 00:02:32,085
HER VISUALS MAKE HIM CHOKE UP

56
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:35,321
Then all we need to do
is add in this sound effect.

57
00:02:35,722 --> 00:02:38,358
AN EX-GIRLFRIEND YOU MIGHT SEE
IN YOUR NIGHTMARE

58
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:40,426
HEH HEH…

59
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:42,762
Even without Han Yu-ju core,

60
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:45,031
you already look quite gorgeous.

61
00:02:45,098 --> 00:02:47,867
So when my looks mix with Han Yu-ju core,

62
00:02:47,934 --> 00:02:50,270
I end up stabbing a dagger
into men's hearts.

63
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:52,038
-A dagger?
-Why would you stab them?

64
00:02:52,105 --> 00:02:55,241
That's not the usual expression, right?

65
00:02:55,308 --> 00:02:58,878
-Stabbing someone can hurt them.
-She doesn't know the drama.

66
00:02:58,945 --> 00:03:00,180
THE LUNATIC EX

67
00:03:00,246 --> 00:03:03,216
-She hasn't seen the drama.
-That's how attractive I am.

68
00:03:03,483 --> 00:03:05,151
HITS THE MARK

69
00:03:05,218 --> 00:03:06,653
She's just bootleg Yu-ju.

70
00:03:09,889 --> 00:03:11,224
-How lovely.
-She squints too much.

71
00:03:11,524 --> 00:03:13,092
SQUINT

72
00:03:13,159 --> 00:03:15,061
Then what really is Han Yu-ju core?

73
00:03:15,128 --> 00:03:19,299
-Any tips for the 2026 Han Yu-ju core fad?
-In 2026?

74
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:21,434
-In 2026?
-How would you do it now?

75
00:03:21,501 --> 00:03:23,436
At this point in time, you'll need money.

76
00:03:23,503 --> 00:03:26,306
-You need money?
-It costs money?

77
00:03:26,372 --> 00:03:29,242
-I need some more gold on me.
-Gold.

78
00:03:29,309 --> 00:03:31,711
If anything, it should be gold-plated.

79
00:03:31,978 --> 00:03:33,246
MUST HAVE SOMETHING SPARKLY

80
00:03:33,313 --> 00:03:35,915
And the hair can't just look natural.

81
00:03:35,982 --> 00:03:40,453
-You need regular deep conditioning.
-That's true.

82
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:43,790
-And the outfit is all about the fabric.
-The fabric.

83
00:03:44,257 --> 00:03:45,158
ALL ABOUT THE DETAILS

84
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:47,193
What do we use? Rayon?

85
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,829
-She brings up the fabric, not the design.
-The fabric.

86
00:03:49,896 --> 00:03:53,066
Fabrics like silk and cashmere.
Throw a sweater over your shoulders.

87
00:03:53,132 --> 00:03:54,734
Those are expensive.

88
00:03:56,536 --> 00:03:59,472
Right. There's a key point
to Han Yu-ju core.

89
00:03:59,539 --> 00:04:01,641
It's what I'm currently wearing,
capri pants.

90
00:04:01,708 --> 00:04:02,742
Capri pants.

91
00:04:02,809 --> 00:04:04,110
-Three-quarter length.
-Yes.

92
00:04:04,177 --> 00:04:06,279
-Three-quarter length.
-That's three-quarter length.

93
00:04:06,346 --> 00:04:08,648
-Three-quarter length?
-Those are in three-quarter length.

94
00:04:08,715 --> 00:04:10,883
You can throw in those items

95
00:04:10,950 --> 00:04:13,419
-to look like a grown woman.
-Capri pants and a blouse.

96
00:04:13,486 --> 00:04:15,588
Deep-conditioning. Gold-plated items.

97
00:04:15,655 --> 00:04:17,423
-Capri pants.
-So, Poong.

98
00:04:17,490 --> 00:04:20,426
What do you think of Jung-an?

99
00:04:20,493 --> 00:04:22,662
I know her now from working together.

100
00:04:23,229 --> 00:04:26,866
I believe
she's one of the greatest actors in Korea.

101
00:04:28,201 --> 00:04:29,869
-Are you just being nice?
-No, I mean it.

102
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:33,706
She has a commanding personality.

103
00:04:33,773 --> 00:04:36,476
-She's a boss and a badass.
-A tough woman.

104
00:04:36,542 --> 00:04:37,710
He's exaggerating.

105
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:41,481
So she has to let herself go completely
to play Han Yu-ju.

106
00:04:41,547 --> 00:04:42,949
-Method acting.
-That's Yu-ju.

107
00:04:43,016 --> 00:04:45,585
That personality she has…

108
00:04:45,652 --> 00:04:46,886
-What's he saying?
-I think…

109
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:48,354
-Is this an attack?
-That's not nice.

110
00:04:49,555 --> 00:04:51,291
I mean, as a person…

111
00:04:51,357 --> 00:04:52,925
I'm not that good at acting.

112
00:04:52,992 --> 00:04:54,661
She says she's not that good at acting.

113
00:04:54,727 --> 00:04:56,729
-He's saying yes.
-She's a great actor.

114
00:04:56,796 --> 00:04:59,866
Well, as a bootleg Yu-ju,

115
00:04:59,932 --> 00:05:02,035
I think that vibe as Han Yu-ju

116
00:05:02,101 --> 00:05:05,071
only comes out
when she's with someone she loves.

117
00:05:07,006 --> 00:05:08,775
I know because I've lived

118
00:05:08,841 --> 00:05:10,777
-in my Han Yu-ju era as a grown woman.
-Her hair.

119
00:05:10,843 --> 00:05:12,979
I know that dreamy mood very well.

120
00:05:13,546 --> 00:05:15,682
Your neck will probably hurt tomorrow.

121
00:05:15,748 --> 00:05:17,517
-Right?
-It's already stiff.

122
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:19,052
BOOTLEG YU-JU'S SIDE EFFECT

123
00:05:19,118 --> 00:05:21,888
-It's not easy to stay like this.
-Many of our chefs

124
00:05:21,954 --> 00:05:25,625
loved the drama <i>Coffee Prince</i> very much.

125
00:05:25,692 --> 00:05:29,062
Jong-won, you must've watched
lots of dramas.

126
00:05:29,128 --> 00:05:30,830
-He loves them a lot.
-And watches too many.

127
00:05:30,897 --> 00:05:33,299
Everyone talks about her character
only as the grown woman,

128
00:05:33,366 --> 00:05:36,202
-but she was also the coolest grown woman.
-That's true.

129
00:05:36,269 --> 00:05:38,771
And back then,
I was always on Team Han Yu-ju.

130
00:05:38,838 --> 00:05:41,674
There were two big names, Jung-an
and Ryeo-won of <i>My Lovely Sam-soon.</i>

131
00:05:41,741 --> 00:05:43,443
But Jong-won was on Team Jung-an.

132
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:44,677
You were?

133
00:05:46,446 --> 00:05:48,114
You'd look great with Ryeo-won.

134
00:05:49,215 --> 00:05:50,049
-What?
-All of a sudden?

135
00:05:50,483 --> 00:05:52,452
ALL OF A SUDDEN?

136
00:05:52,785 --> 00:05:53,953
HEADACHE

137
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,255
-With Ryeo-won?
-In terms of their looks. Right?

138
00:05:56,589 --> 00:05:58,458
SHE'S TOO UNPREDICTABLE

139
00:05:58,524 --> 00:06:00,426
I always thought you were the best.

140
00:06:00,727 --> 00:06:02,061
MOVED

141
00:06:02,128 --> 00:06:05,031
-She was a huge hit too.
-Yes, she released lots of great songs.

142
00:06:05,098 --> 00:06:06,432
There was "Letter" and a lot more.

143
00:06:06,499 --> 00:06:08,234
When I performed at the army,

144
00:06:08,301 --> 00:06:11,070
I performed really hard,
thinking I'd build the nation with them.

145
00:06:11,137 --> 00:06:12,338
Building what nation?

146
00:06:12,405 --> 00:06:15,441
-Not "protecting" the nation?
-Protecting the nation.

147
00:06:15,508 --> 00:06:17,110
It's already been built, so protect it.

148
00:06:17,176 --> 00:06:19,512
-I performed with all that I had.
-Even harder.

149
00:06:19,579 --> 00:06:21,414
You know what?

150
00:06:21,481 --> 00:06:25,685
There's a male celebrity
who said she was his first love.

151
00:06:25,752 --> 00:06:27,453
He's an actor.

152
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:31,224
-He left this on the coffee truck.
-A love confession?

153
00:06:31,290 --> 00:06:32,959
"My first love, Han Yu-ju.

154
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:36,796
Did you think I wouldn't know
if you got a new name? Hope you're happy.

155
00:06:36,863 --> 00:06:39,766
Actor Chae Jung-an
is banned from twerking."

156
00:06:39,832 --> 00:06:41,667
-Twerking?
-Twerking?

157
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:43,636
-Twerking?
-And he left his name.

158
00:06:43,703 --> 00:06:44,670
Gong Yoo.

159
00:06:45,972 --> 00:06:46,873
Gong Yoo's first love.

160
00:06:47,206 --> 00:06:48,674
TWERKING?

161
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:52,545
He left that on the banner.
"Banned from twerking."

162
00:06:52,612 --> 00:06:54,347
A BANNER AT HER SET

163
00:06:54,414 --> 00:06:55,982
You twerk?

164
00:06:56,048 --> 00:06:57,717
No, not recently.

165
00:06:57,784 --> 00:06:59,685
-"Not recently"?
-She used to.

166
00:06:59,752 --> 00:07:01,053
-He's seen it.
-I quit it already.

167
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:03,055
-He must've seen it.
-She used to twerk.

168
00:07:03,122 --> 00:07:05,024
-Tell us the story.
-Twerking is hard.

169
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:07,894
I made a reservation at a restaurant
that had a round table.

170
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:10,463
Gong Yoo, another friend, and I,
the three of us went to eat.

171
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:13,900
They let us choose our own music,
so we played something.

172
00:07:13,966 --> 00:07:18,004
At that time, I was wondering
what it truly means to be cool.

173
00:07:18,070 --> 00:07:21,340
So I had the cool attitude
to just get up and dance

174
00:07:21,407 --> 00:07:23,109
if the music made me.

175
00:07:23,176 --> 00:07:27,447
-I was very resistant to dancing.
-"Resistant"?

176
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:28,748
CAN CONNECT(?)

177
00:07:28,815 --> 00:07:31,717
It was an open kitchen,
but the chefs were all inside.

178
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:34,720
Gong Yoo and our friend were there,
and I suddenly got up

179
00:07:34,787 --> 00:07:36,322
to twerk very briefly.

180
00:07:36,389 --> 00:07:37,690
-To the music?
-Yes.

181
00:07:37,757 --> 00:07:39,292
I hoped they wouldn't notice.

182
00:07:39,358 --> 00:07:40,560
How can they not?

183
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:43,196
-No one else was there.
-It was just the three of you.

184
00:07:43,262 --> 00:07:45,465
I hoped they'd be cool about it
and just let me be.

185
00:07:45,531 --> 00:07:48,501
You were cool with it,
so you hoped they'd be too.

186
00:07:48,568 --> 00:07:49,902
Suddenly, Gong Yoo said,

187
00:07:50,403 --> 00:07:52,338
"Don't ever dance out there."

188
00:07:52,405 --> 00:07:55,074
-"I'm so irritated. I want to unsee that."
-Irritated?

189
00:07:55,408 --> 00:07:58,444
EXTREMELY ANGRY

190
00:07:58,511 --> 00:08:00,079
And then, he sent me this text.

191
00:08:00,146 --> 00:08:02,915
"Don't ever go anywhere and twerk.

192
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:04,417
I still remember your dance."

193
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:06,385
-He remembers.
-He keeps thinking about it.

194
00:08:06,452 --> 00:08:08,421
He remembered the way I danced.

195
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:10,389
I personally think

196
00:08:10,456 --> 00:08:12,625
he went home and did the dance alone.

197
00:08:13,726 --> 00:08:14,861
At home?

198
00:08:14,927 --> 00:08:17,563
-I know it. He must've done it.
-Out of curiosity?

199
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:19,098
How did you twerk?

200
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:22,502
I kind of understand
why Gong Yoo said what he said.

201
00:08:22,568 --> 00:08:25,071
-You're more evil.
-Wait.

202
00:08:25,137 --> 00:08:28,207
It looks like Sang-uk has
a lot going on in his mind.

203
00:08:28,274 --> 00:08:29,842
-She's a lot of fun.
-She is?

204
00:08:29,909 --> 00:08:31,878
You're watching her
like you were a viewer.

205
00:08:31,944 --> 00:08:34,313
I really didn't know

206
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:37,149
she was like this. Truly.

207
00:08:37,216 --> 00:08:38,451
-I…
-"Like this"?

208
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:39,886
-Wait.
-What do you mean by that?

209
00:08:39,952 --> 00:08:41,220
She seemed calm.

210
00:08:41,287 --> 00:08:44,257
Because back then, the host,
Lee Kyung-kyu, hated it when I talked.

211
00:08:46,826 --> 00:08:48,761
THE EMERGENCY LIGHT IS BUSY AT WORK

212
00:08:48,828 --> 00:08:52,164
-He'd cut me off when I talked.
-Well, I…

213
00:08:53,399 --> 00:08:55,968
-Did Kyung-kyu tell you to stop?
-Yes.

214
00:08:56,035 --> 00:08:59,705
But he commended me by the end,
saying I improved a lot.

215
00:08:59,772 --> 00:09:02,008
-Let's cook very well today.
-Let's do that.

216
00:09:02,074 --> 00:09:04,243
WE'LL REPAY YOU WITH THE DISHES

217
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:08,347
She also said she knows
a lot about a chef's life.

218
00:09:08,414 --> 00:09:09,882
-A chef's life.
-How so?

219
00:09:09,949 --> 00:09:11,551
I have a younger sister,

220
00:09:11,617 --> 00:09:13,753
and she married an Italian chef.

221
00:09:13,819 --> 00:09:15,755
-Your brother-in-law?
-My brother-in-law.

222
00:09:15,821 --> 00:09:18,925
-You never eat dinner on time, right?
-No.

223
00:09:18,991 --> 00:09:21,427
So they always have to eat
a late-night snack.

224
00:09:21,494 --> 00:09:22,595
NODDING

225
00:09:22,662 --> 00:09:24,497
That makes you prone to adult diseases.

226
00:09:26,499 --> 00:09:29,468
So my brother-in-law goes running often.

227
00:09:29,535 --> 00:09:32,271
Do you see some chefs
who should start running?

228
00:09:32,338 --> 00:09:33,506
But you're so slender.

229
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:35,041
-Me?
-Hyun-suk.

230
00:09:35,107 --> 00:09:36,642
You've taken good care of yourself.

231
00:09:36,709 --> 00:09:39,178
-He has a bit of a bump down here.
-Chef Hyun-suk.

232
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:40,379
RIGHT HERE

233
00:09:40,446 --> 00:09:42,381
I WON'T LET THIS GO

234
00:09:42,448 --> 00:09:44,584
But do you see who should start running?

235
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:46,485
-There are a few.
-Tell them the harsh truth.

236
00:09:46,552 --> 00:09:47,820
They're across from each other.

237
00:09:47,887 --> 00:09:49,989
-Across from each other? Right.
-Right.

238
00:09:50,056 --> 00:09:53,526
-It's you.
-Wait, he runs. One of us runs.

239
00:09:54,527 --> 00:09:56,796
I've been maintaining this weight
because I run.

240
00:09:56,862 --> 00:10:00,132
I went to my brother-in-law's restaurant
before they got married,

241
00:10:00,199 --> 00:10:02,134
and he made me <i>vongole </i>pasta.

242
00:10:02,201 --> 00:10:05,571
The moment I had it,
I could sense his character.

243
00:10:05,638 --> 00:10:08,240
I see. You noticed his character
in the <i>vongole </i>pasta?

244
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:10,776
SHE EVALUATED HIS CHARACTER,
NOT THE TASTE?

245
00:10:10,843 --> 00:10:13,646
-How do you sense his character?
-What was it like?

246
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,848
-What's my pasta like?
-I could sense

247
00:10:15,915 --> 00:10:19,552
the innocence and kindness he had.

248
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:24,123
So I knew that my sister
would get to live with a sweet guy.

249
00:10:24,323 --> 00:10:25,758
…TOTALLY SERIOUS

250
00:10:25,825 --> 00:10:26,859
After you try their food,

251
00:10:26,926 --> 00:10:30,730
please evaluate
what our chefs' characters are like.

252
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:33,966
WHAT WILL SHE SAY ABOUT OUR CHEFS?

253
00:10:34,033 --> 00:10:35,601
What kind of ingredients

254
00:10:35,668 --> 00:10:38,337
does Jung-an, an actor without a filter,
keep in her fridge?

255
00:10:38,404 --> 00:10:41,540
It's time to open it and see.

256
00:10:41,607 --> 00:10:43,676
You've taken great care of yourself,

257
00:10:43,743 --> 00:10:47,480
so I'm sure many women
are curious to see what you eat.

258
00:10:47,546 --> 00:10:49,782
Jung-an, someone who's the same today
as 20 years ago.

259
00:10:49,849 --> 00:10:52,852
Let's find out what she eats.

260
00:10:52,918 --> 00:10:56,222
-We present Jung-an's fridge!
-Fridge!

261
00:10:56,288 --> 00:10:57,390
-Fridge!
-Fridge!

262
00:10:57,456 --> 00:10:58,991
-Whoa.
-That's a lot.

263
00:10:59,058 --> 00:11:00,926
-She has lots of stuff.
-She does.

264
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:03,562
PRESENTING JUNG-AN'S FRIDGE

265
00:11:03,963 --> 00:11:06,165
NEATLY ORGANIZED AND ABUNDANT FRIDGE

266
00:11:06,232 --> 00:11:08,367
It's neatly organized.

267
00:11:08,434 --> 00:11:10,569
-The top shelf was as I expected.
-Look here.

268
00:11:10,636 --> 00:11:13,773
-Cosmetic products.
-It's like a dermatologist's office.

269
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:16,676
-So these are what you use.
-There are more.

270
00:11:16,742 --> 00:11:19,145
It's been too hot lately,

271
00:11:19,211 --> 00:11:22,515
so I stick toner pads on my face
to cool my face down when I get home.

272
00:11:22,581 --> 00:11:24,050
-Cooling pads?
-Yes.

273
00:11:24,116 --> 00:11:25,918
-For the heat.
-It's hot these days,

274
00:11:25,985 --> 00:11:27,286
and at times, you just get fired up.

275
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:28,754
We do.

276
00:11:28,821 --> 00:11:30,856
-I stick it on my face when that happens.
-To calm down?

277
00:11:30,923 --> 00:11:34,827
And a few of my friends
get flushed when they drink.

278
00:11:34,894 --> 00:11:37,029
So my drunken habit
is putting those pads on them.

279
00:11:37,096 --> 00:11:38,698
That's your drunken habit?

280
00:11:38,764 --> 00:11:40,499
They look uglier when they get drunk.

281
00:11:40,733 --> 00:11:41,934
SURPRISED

282
00:11:42,001 --> 00:11:45,438
So I grab the toner pads
and put them on their faces.

283
00:11:45,504 --> 00:11:48,240
Jung-an won the pageant
for women with great skin.

284
00:11:48,307 --> 00:11:51,577
You must have a sense of duty
to keep your skin looking great.

285
00:11:51,644 --> 00:11:54,413
I find myself paying more attention.

286
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:57,883
-What's this midface exercise that you do?
-"Midface exercise"?

287
00:11:57,950 --> 00:11:59,618
-It's important.
-You know.

288
00:11:59,685 --> 00:12:03,322
The key to looking younger
is apparently your midface length.

289
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:07,226
-I see.
-I thought Sung-ju looked really young.

290
00:12:07,293 --> 00:12:08,461
A young-looking face.

291
00:12:08,527 --> 00:12:10,830
-Totally.
-It wasn't that you had a tiny face,

292
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:13,866
but you used to have
a very short midface, didn't you?

293
00:12:13,933 --> 00:12:15,968
But you know
that it's longer than before, right?

294
00:12:18,170 --> 00:12:19,605
Right?

295
00:12:19,672 --> 00:12:20,906
SOMEHOW FEELS SATISFYING(?)

296
00:12:20,973 --> 00:12:23,476
-But you still look young. It's so short.
-It's that short.

297
00:12:23,542 --> 00:12:25,678
-It has to be short.
-So did it sag?

298
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,880
-Short, right?
-It gets droopy.

299
00:12:27,947 --> 00:12:29,381
Why are you laughing at me?

300
00:12:29,448 --> 00:12:32,918
-Can I make it shorter? How?
-You can exercise and make it shorter?

301
00:12:32,985 --> 00:12:34,754
It's been talked about, so don't you know?

302
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:36,455
-Wait, how? We don't know.
-No.

303
00:12:36,522 --> 00:12:38,124
It makes you look really bad.

304
00:12:38,190 --> 00:12:40,025
A tiger goes "roar," right?

305
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:41,460
-Roar.
-Roar.

306
00:12:41,527 --> 00:12:43,596
-But you're moving all of your face.
-Roar.

307
00:12:43,662 --> 00:12:45,564
Move just your cheeks. Roar.

308
00:12:45,631 --> 00:12:47,366
-Roar.
-Roar.

309
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,534
Roar.

310
00:12:48,701 --> 00:12:50,903
A CULTURE SHOCK

311
00:12:51,337 --> 00:12:52,772
IT'S RIGHT UP MY ALLEY

312
00:12:52,838 --> 00:12:54,774
Do it repeatedly
for 30 seconds to one minute.

313
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:56,575
All you have to do is "roar."

314
00:12:57,209 --> 00:13:01,781
A VARIETY OF BAD-LOOKING FACES

315
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:05,851
My cheeks go up when I smile,
so does smiling count?

316
00:13:05,918 --> 00:13:09,188
-So that's the midface exercise.
-Yes, that's it.

317
00:13:09,255 --> 00:13:10,222
Sang-uk did it too.

318
00:13:10,589 --> 00:13:12,558
EMBARRASSED…

319
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,126
Can you roar?

320
00:13:14,193 --> 00:13:15,094
Roar!

321
00:13:16,562 --> 00:13:19,865
The midface gets saggy over time.
It's just the aging process.

322
00:13:20,099 --> 00:13:21,467
QUITE EFFECTIVE

323
00:13:21,534 --> 00:13:23,335
But by our age,

324
00:13:23,402 --> 00:13:25,471
I think it's better to age gracefully.

325
00:13:25,538 --> 00:13:28,340
Even those who age gracefully
are all roaring behind your back.

326
00:13:29,542 --> 00:13:31,043
-Yes.
-Yes, do that too.

327
00:13:31,110 --> 00:13:33,179
-Do it when you're told to.
-They'd do it at home.

328
00:13:33,245 --> 00:13:35,481
You don't think you'll do it,
but you'll do it at home.

329
00:13:35,548 --> 00:13:37,082
-Everyone will.
-And daily.

330
00:13:37,149 --> 00:13:39,251
-I'll do my best.
-Do it whenever you're reminded.

331
00:13:39,318 --> 00:13:41,120
-Roar.
-It doesn't even cost money.

332
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:43,155
JOINING THE ROARING

333
00:13:43,355 --> 00:13:44,890
FEELING PROUD

334
00:13:44,957 --> 00:13:46,692
Do you have a morning routine?

335
00:13:46,759 --> 00:13:49,195
I drink a cup of lukewarm salted water.

336
00:13:49,261 --> 00:13:51,297
-Lukewarm salted water?
-Yes.

337
00:13:51,363 --> 00:13:52,531
-Salt.
-I see lots of salt.

338
00:13:52,598 --> 00:13:55,301
-These are all salt.
-But don't use coarse salt.

339
00:13:55,367 --> 00:13:56,602
-Any salt?
-Not bay salt.

340
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:57,903
It's not just any salt.

341
00:13:57,970 --> 00:14:01,740
-Like Himalayan pink salt.
-Rock salt.

342
00:14:01,807 --> 00:14:04,510
Something with lots of minerals.

343
00:14:04,577 --> 00:14:06,879
-I use a very small amount of it.
-A very small amount.

344
00:14:06,946 --> 00:14:09,481
-Then I chug it.
-You chug it?

345
00:14:09,548 --> 00:14:10,850
It makes you feel great.

346
00:14:10,916 --> 00:14:15,020
I've recently been
feeling a bit faint in the morning,

347
00:14:15,087 --> 00:14:18,157
and salt is bad for patients
with high blood pressure.

348
00:14:18,224 --> 00:14:19,892
-Yes.
-So I took it the other way.

349
00:14:19,959 --> 00:14:20,826
SHE DIDN'T…

350
00:14:20,893 --> 00:14:23,262
I have low blood pressure,
so I think salt works for me.

351
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:25,231
QUIRKY

352
00:14:25,297 --> 00:14:27,099
-It depends on the person.
-So I eat

353
00:14:27,166 --> 00:14:30,169
some eggs with the leftover salt.

354
00:14:30,236 --> 00:14:32,438
You asked what I eat for breakfast, right?

355
00:14:32,504 --> 00:14:35,441
-I see eggs here. She has some here.
-I eat eggs.

356
00:14:35,507 --> 00:14:38,143
I had to wait to buy those eggs.

357
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:39,912
Are these special?

358
00:14:39,979 --> 00:14:42,548
The yolks are orange.

359
00:14:42,815 --> 00:14:45,918
THE YOLKS ARE IN DIFFERENT COLORS
DEPENDING ON THE CHICKEN FEED

360
00:14:45,985 --> 00:14:46,952
Do you fry them?

361
00:14:47,019 --> 00:14:49,722
-I like that, but I boil them now.
-Boiled eggs.

362
00:14:49,788 --> 00:14:53,893
-I like the act of boiling the eggs.
-The act of boiling?

363
00:14:53,959 --> 00:14:56,228
The sound of eggs boiling at 100°C?

364
00:14:56,295 --> 00:15:00,833
It feels like
I'm doing something nice for myself.

365
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,935
-When you boil eggs?
-Yes.

366
00:15:03,002 --> 00:15:04,069
The third shelf.

367
00:15:04,136 --> 00:15:06,438
-What's this? Right?
-Tomato sauce.

368
00:15:06,505 --> 00:15:08,674
-Do you use these to cook?
-Yes.

369
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:10,009
Do you cook?

370
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:11,677
When I don't feel like delivery food

371
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:13,612
and want to make
a homemade meal for myself.

372
00:15:13,679 --> 00:15:15,748
I had that feeling about a month ago.

373
00:15:15,814 --> 00:15:17,316
You had a feeling, but it's not open.

374
00:15:17,383 --> 00:15:18,250
It's new.

375
00:15:18,317 --> 00:15:21,420
The weather was too hot,
so I didn't feel like cooking.

376
00:15:21,487 --> 00:15:24,123
So you either order or cook your food
depending on your mood?

377
00:15:24,189 --> 00:15:25,891
I like to follow my feelings.

378
00:15:25,958 --> 00:15:28,227
-My feelings.
-She has these specific feelings.

379
00:15:28,294 --> 00:15:31,163
Why do you prefer to have food delivered
instead of cooking at home?

380
00:15:31,230 --> 00:15:34,867
Shopping for groceries to make myself food

381
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,268
is stressful to me.

382
00:15:36,869 --> 00:15:38,203
When it comes to food,

383
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:41,173
I don't want the stress
of cleaning and throwing out leftovers.

384
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:45,010
It's more beneficial for me
to get high-quality food delivered.

385
00:15:46,078 --> 00:15:47,246
High-quality delivery food.

386
00:15:47,313 --> 00:15:49,815
-Something high-quality.
-What do you usually eat?

387
00:15:49,882 --> 00:15:51,116
What's high-quality?

388
00:15:51,183 --> 00:15:53,819
I often eat vegan dishes on the weekends.

389
00:15:53,886 --> 00:15:54,853
Such as?

390
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:57,723
Sandwiches made with <i>namul,</i>
seasoned greens.

391
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:58,857
I also love soup.

392
00:15:58,924 --> 00:16:00,926
<i>Dogani-tang, gom-tang.</i>

393
00:16:01,694 --> 00:16:04,430
I pretty much splurge my fortune on those.

394
00:16:04,496 --> 00:16:06,732
-Do you eat fried chicken?
-I don't.

395
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:08,334
-How about pizza?
-I eat pizza.

396
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:10,602
I used to eat
lots of spicy braised chicken,

397
00:16:10,669 --> 00:16:12,538
but when I got my constitution checked,

398
00:16:12,604 --> 00:16:15,074
I was told to stay away
from chicken and duck.

399
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:16,775
They can make me even more hyper.

400
00:16:17,009 --> 00:16:19,578
TO PREVENT HYPERACTIVITY(?)

401
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:22,047
-I'm focusing on beef and pork.
-They make her hyper.

402
00:16:22,114 --> 00:16:23,782
What's next?

403
00:16:23,849 --> 00:16:25,951
-Some cheese.
-We found some cheese.

404
00:16:26,018 --> 00:16:29,188
I love to fry eggs with a slice of cheese.

405
00:16:29,254 --> 00:16:31,724
-With sliced cheese?
-Yes, it gets scorched

406
00:16:31,790 --> 00:16:34,860
<i>-with a nice crust.</i>
<i>-On top of the cheese?</i>

407
00:16:34,927 --> 00:16:36,362
<i>and you don't even need salt.</i>

408
00:16:36,428 --> 00:16:38,297
It's salty and delicious.

409
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:39,498
AGREED

410
00:16:40,065 --> 00:16:41,633
What's this?

411
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:45,871
-Hummus?
-Yes, it's a dip.

412
00:16:45,938 --> 00:16:48,073
Is this a Chinese sauce?

413
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:50,576
-Chili paste.
-That one.

414
00:16:50,642 --> 00:16:53,445
My friend brought it over to make me food,

415
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:55,014
then disappeared.

416
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,148
"Disappeared"?

417
00:16:56,215 --> 00:16:57,349
I can't reach my friend.

418
00:16:57,416 --> 00:16:58,884
I think I've used it once.

419
00:16:58,951 --> 00:17:02,388
-Yes, you did. It must be spicy.
-It is.

420
00:17:02,454 --> 00:17:05,524
So I used just a tiny bit
to add just a bit of spice.

421
00:17:05,591 --> 00:17:06,692
Do you enjoy spicy food?

422
00:17:06,759 --> 00:17:08,027
I don't do well with it,

423
00:17:08,093 --> 00:17:09,628
but I find it delicious.

424
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:13,265
You eat spicy food,
but you don't go looking for it.

425
00:17:13,332 --> 00:17:14,700
-That makes me hyper too.
-That too?

426
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:18,404
I guess her constitution
doesn't work with anything hot.

427
00:17:18,470 --> 00:17:20,239
-Right.
-From what she said,

428
00:17:20,305 --> 00:17:23,542
it looks like she avoids food
that'll become trouble later.

429
00:17:23,609 --> 00:17:24,777
Because of my intestines.

430
00:17:24,843 --> 00:17:27,546
Is there anything you eat for gut health?

431
00:17:27,613 --> 00:17:28,914
I love <i>nurungji,</i> scorched rice.

432
00:17:28,981 --> 00:17:30,049
<i>-Nurungji.</i>
<i>-Nurungji.</i>

433
00:17:30,115 --> 00:17:32,317
-I have a lot over there.
<i>-Nurungji.</i>

434
00:17:32,384 --> 00:17:35,554
I love going to pot rice places
because I love the scorched rice.

435
00:17:35,621 --> 00:17:37,056
Is <i>nurungji</i> good for your gut?

436
00:17:37,122 --> 00:17:38,090
Yes.

437
00:17:38,290 --> 00:17:39,191
CHUCKLE

438
00:17:39,258 --> 00:17:40,993
Doesn't it have digestive enzymes?

439
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,327
-These are all <i>nurungji.</i>
-Don't they?

440
00:17:43,028 --> 00:17:45,064
-And this.
-That's <i>nurungji</i> too.

441
00:17:45,130 --> 00:17:47,766
-She has so much <i>nurungji</i>.
-You have a lot.

442
00:17:47,833 --> 00:17:51,036
Our ancestors were so wise
for eating<i> nurungji</i> after meals

443
00:17:51,103 --> 00:17:53,338
because they have digestive enzymes.

444
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:55,374
CARBS DISINTEGRATE IN HEAT
AND HELP WITH ABSORPTION

445
00:17:55,441 --> 00:17:58,210
Anyway, when I eat it,
I can feel my serotonin rushing.

446
00:17:58,277 --> 00:17:59,845
-It makes her feel good.
-She's happy.

447
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:02,414
-She's taking care of herself.
-You must love it.

448
00:18:02,481 --> 00:18:05,584
-Do you also enjoy wine?
-Yes.

449
00:18:05,651 --> 00:18:07,152
I like to have a drink with my meals,

450
00:18:07,219 --> 00:18:10,222
and I feel like wine
helps with my digestion.

451
00:18:10,289 --> 00:18:11,790
So that's your digestive medicine.

452
00:18:11,857 --> 00:18:15,360
-I think she just likes to drink.
-She seems to like it.

453
00:18:15,427 --> 00:18:18,897
Is there a bar snack
or dessert you like to eat with wine?

454
00:18:19,465 --> 00:18:20,466
I don't like sweet things.

455
00:18:20,532 --> 00:18:21,967
You don't like sweet things.

456
00:18:22,034 --> 00:18:24,436
-Those who drink don't like sweets.
-She likes to drink.

457
00:18:24,636 --> 00:18:26,205
CAN CONNECT

458
00:18:26,805 --> 00:18:28,540
Among Jung-an's drunken habits,

459
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:30,142
there's headbutting.

460
00:18:30,209 --> 00:18:32,744
-Headbutting? "Come here."
-Headbutting. Is it true?

461
00:18:32,811 --> 00:18:35,547
It was when I was much younger.

462
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:39,818
Let's say I'm sitting next
to someone really attractive.

463
00:18:39,885 --> 00:18:41,987
-Someone really nice.
-So does she headbutt him?

464
00:18:42,054 --> 00:18:43,589
When I'm drunk, I'd just

465
00:18:44,156 --> 00:18:45,224
headbutt him, out of nowhere.

466
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:47,860
-Right here?
-Yes, because I like him that much.

467
00:18:47,926 --> 00:18:50,996
-Because you like him?
-Because I like them so much.

468
00:18:51,063 --> 00:18:53,665
-Like how you want to bite cute things.
-Because they're so cute.

469
00:18:53,732 --> 00:18:55,367
It's a sign of interest, right?

470
00:18:55,434 --> 00:18:56,869
-For that person.
-Yes.

471
00:18:56,935 --> 00:18:58,704
When I did that, the person left me.

472
00:18:59,905 --> 00:19:00,839
It didn't work.

473
00:19:00,906 --> 00:19:04,643
Did your chili sauce friend disappear
because you headbutted them?

474
00:19:05,777 --> 00:19:07,112
Do you think that's why?

475
00:19:07,379 --> 00:19:08,380
YES…

476
00:19:08,447 --> 00:19:10,983
-That's not it.
-That's not it?

477
00:19:11,049 --> 00:19:12,851
And down here.

478
00:19:12,918 --> 00:19:14,753
-Avocado.
-Tangerines and apples.

479
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:17,156
Apples. Many fruits and veggies.

480
00:19:17,222 --> 00:19:20,325
-Cucumbers. And carrots.
-Bean sprouts.

481
00:19:20,392 --> 00:19:23,095
What's on the top shelf of the freezer?

482
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:26,231
-Bread and <i>tteok,</i> rice cake.
-Bread.

483
00:19:26,298 --> 00:19:28,567
-I love <i>tteok.</i>
-You do?

484
00:19:28,634 --> 00:19:31,203
Are these seafood?

485
00:19:31,270 --> 00:19:33,672
-Octopus.
-<i>Gulbi, </i>dried yellow corvina.

486
00:19:33,739 --> 00:19:36,341
-And octopus.
-<i>Nurungji </i>tastes great with <i>gulbi.</i>

487
00:19:36,408 --> 00:19:37,876
-That's a good pair.
-That's nice.

488
00:19:37,943 --> 00:19:40,345
-<i>Bori-gulbi.</i>
-Yes, <i>bori-gulbi.</i>

489
00:19:40,412 --> 00:19:41,680
There are lots of things here.

490
00:19:41,747 --> 00:19:43,549
Some dried squid.

491
00:19:43,615 --> 00:19:46,084
Do you remember how squid
was expensive earlier this year?

492
00:19:46,151 --> 00:19:49,188
-I got them when they were expensive.
-They were expensive.

493
00:19:49,254 --> 00:19:52,591
People usually stock up
when they're the cheapest.

494
00:19:52,658 --> 00:19:54,960
Why did you get them
while they were expensive?

495
00:19:55,027 --> 00:19:56,361
I thought it'd rise even more.

496
00:19:56,428 --> 00:19:58,597
She thought the market price would rise.

497
00:19:58,664 --> 00:20:01,366
-It's like an investment.
-It was a "squidvestment."

498
00:20:01,433 --> 00:20:02,868
I thought it'd rise some more.

499
00:20:02,935 --> 00:20:05,137
-At least she had the space.
-The squids.

500
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:08,307
That's all for Jung-an's fridge.

501
00:20:08,373 --> 00:20:10,275
FINISHED CHECKING OUT JUNG-AN'S FRIDGE!

502
00:20:10,342 --> 00:20:13,879
What does she want to eat today?

503
00:20:13,946 --> 00:20:16,215
Show us her orders!

504
00:20:16,281 --> 00:20:18,417
-They must be difficult.
-Jung-an's orders.

505
00:20:20,118 --> 00:20:22,421
-The Grown Woman, Han Yu-ju Core.
-The Grown Woman, Han Yu-ju Core.

506
00:20:22,487 --> 00:20:24,656
-What do you mean?
-What's that?

507
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:28,293
Han Yu-ju has now become middle-aged,

508
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:29,761
so she has no appetite.

509
00:20:29,828 --> 00:20:32,764
And many guys have already bought her
all kinds of good food before.

510
00:20:32,831 --> 00:20:36,501
-She's tried them all, so nothing's new.
-Right.

511
00:20:36,568 --> 00:20:38,303
So I want something adultcore,

512
00:20:38,370 --> 00:20:42,641
something that'll bring back
Han Yu-ju's lost appetite.

513
00:20:42,708 --> 00:20:44,476
-Something fancy yet demure.
-Yes.

514
00:20:44,543 --> 00:20:46,345
Something that Yu-ju would eat.

515
00:20:46,411 --> 00:20:48,714
The second order is revealed too.

516
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:50,616
Eats Like a Kid, Chae Jung-an Core.

517
00:20:50,682 --> 00:20:54,186
I take my nutritional supplements and all,

518
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:58,223
but when I get stressed out
or on my cheat days,

519
00:20:58,290 --> 00:21:00,692
I love to eat
<i>tteokbokki, ramyeon, </i>and <i>gimbap.</i>

520
00:21:00,759 --> 00:21:02,527
<i>Gimbap</i> is my favorite.

521
00:21:02,594 --> 00:21:04,396
-I see.
-You do?

522
00:21:04,463 --> 00:21:07,432
I want to eat something
that I can enjoy with my friends,

523
00:21:07,499 --> 00:21:09,968
something that'll give me
a blood sugar spike.

524
00:21:10,035 --> 00:21:11,436
Something delicious.

525
00:21:11,503 --> 00:21:15,073
If she eats like a kid,
she must mean <i>bunsik,</i> snack foods.

526
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:17,442
Four people remain after our last episode.

527
00:21:17,509 --> 00:21:20,078
We should give Eun-yeong a chance.

528
00:21:20,145 --> 00:21:21,680
Although she's a bootleg.

529
00:21:21,747 --> 00:21:27,252
I've studied Han Yu-ju core,
the grown woman aesthetic for life.

530
00:21:27,319 --> 00:21:29,288
I should join that round.

531
00:21:29,354 --> 00:21:31,423
Yes, that one is for you.

532
00:21:31,490 --> 00:21:34,493
Chef Eun-yeong takes Han Yu-ju core.

533
00:21:34,559 --> 00:21:36,328
I'll go

534
00:21:36,395 --> 00:21:38,930
-for Eats Like a Kid, Chae Jung-an Core.
-Emergency.

535
00:21:38,997 --> 00:21:41,133
-It's an emergency.
-Poong joins the second one.

536
00:21:41,199 --> 00:21:45,570
-I really wanted to try his food.
-I can cook for those who eat like a kid.

537
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:47,072
