with the long, tiny spoon.

629
00:25:20,719 --> 00:25:22,053
He's right.

630
00:25:22,120 --> 00:25:23,755
With a cocktail umbrella.

631
00:25:23,822 --> 00:25:26,424
-And a wafer cookie.
-That's right.

632
00:25:26,491 --> 00:25:28,960
You pick your teeth with that
as you walk out.

633
00:25:29,027 --> 00:25:31,296
-Like Chow Yun-fat.
-Chow Yun-fat?

634
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:33,331
With the cocktail umbrella.

635
00:25:33,398 --> 00:25:35,600
-That was a thing back then.
-Yes.

636
00:25:35,667 --> 00:25:37,135
But she doesn't like sweet things,

637
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:38,770
so I'll make one with food.

638
00:25:38,837 --> 00:25:40,038
-What?
-With food?

639
00:25:40,105 --> 00:25:42,607
-You'll serve your food in a cup?
-A parfait made with food.

640
00:25:42,674 --> 00:25:44,142
Like a rice bowl in a cup?

641
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:46,077
-Rice bowl in a cup?
-It's like that.

642
00:25:46,144 --> 00:25:48,280
-You killed it.
-It sounds so tacky.

643
00:25:48,346 --> 00:25:51,950
Parfait is a dish served
in a long cup in layers.

644
00:25:52,017 --> 00:25:55,053
-So I'll create eleven different layers.
-Eleven?

645
00:25:55,120 --> 00:25:57,989
-Eleven?
-<i>Parfait</i> means "perfect" in French.

646
00:25:58,056 --> 00:26:00,325
<i>Parfait.</i> So I'll make a perfect dish

647
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:02,327
-for someone gorgeous like you.
-"Perfect."

648
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:03,995
-I see.
-That's why I prepared this.

649
00:26:04,062 --> 00:26:05,797
I'm already getting excited.

650
00:26:05,864 --> 00:26:08,066
And now, let us begin
the cook-off for Jung-an,

651
00:26:08,133 --> 00:26:10,969
The Grown Woman, Han Yu-ju Core.

652
00:26:11,036 --> 00:26:15,040
"My twin sister was actually Han Yu-ju."

653
00:26:15,106 --> 00:26:18,577
The self-proclaimed Yu-ju's doppelgänger,
Chef Park Eun-yeong.

654
00:26:18,643 --> 00:26:23,214
But he's here to crush
the midface of the bootleg Yu-ju,

655
00:26:23,281 --> 00:26:27,452
-her protector, Chef Son Jong-won.
-Crushing her midface?

656
00:26:28,186 --> 00:26:32,023
Which one of them will satisfy
Han Yu-ju, the grown woman?

657
00:26:32,090 --> 00:26:34,960
Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!

658
00:26:38,363 --> 00:26:40,999
GETTING INTO CHARACTER FOR FULL IMMERSION

659
00:26:41,366 --> 00:26:44,269
THE OUTSPOKEN AND BRAVE WOMAN,
PARK EUN-YEONG

660
00:26:44,836 --> 00:26:46,404
Why is there so much stuff?

661
00:26:48,773 --> 00:26:49,908
What's that? Nutella?

662
00:26:49,975 --> 00:26:51,543
Manuka honey.

663
00:26:51,610 --> 00:26:52,811
-Honey?
-Yes.

664
00:26:52,877 --> 00:26:54,379
-Soy sauce.
-Soy sauce.

665
00:26:54,446 --> 00:26:56,247
That honey also tastes bitter.

666
00:26:56,314 --> 00:26:58,149
-She tastes it.
-A bit.

667
00:26:59,050 --> 00:26:59,884
PORK NECK

668
00:27:00,585 --> 00:27:01,920
MIX SAUCE WITH PORK

669
00:27:01,987 --> 00:27:03,488
That pork neck.

670
00:27:03,555 --> 00:27:06,558
-It's meat marinated in soy sauce.
-It's pork neck.

671
00:27:06,625 --> 00:27:09,060
I'm making <i>chashu</i> in Hong Kong style.

672
00:27:09,327 --> 00:27:11,529
A GROWN WOMAN WHO HAS STUDIED IN HONG KONG

673
00:27:12,130 --> 00:27:13,098
FLIP

674
00:27:13,465 --> 00:27:16,601
THE CALM GUY EVEN WHEN HE'S FLUSTERED,
SON JONG-WON

675
00:27:17,836 --> 00:27:19,404
-Corn.
-You're steaming corn?

676
00:27:19,471 --> 00:27:22,040
He's starting out by steaming corn.

677
00:27:22,107 --> 00:27:23,441
Can you steam them that quickly?

678
00:27:23,508 --> 00:27:24,976
-It's been steamed before.
-Really?

679
00:27:25,043 --> 00:27:26,911
Yes, I froze the steamed ones.

680
00:27:26,978 --> 00:27:28,780
He must need them for the parfait.

681
00:27:28,847 --> 00:27:31,383
That's pasta, and it looks unique.

682
00:27:31,449 --> 00:27:32,384
That's pasta?

683
00:27:32,884 --> 00:27:34,953
It's interesting that
he's using pasta for the parfait.

684
00:27:35,020 --> 00:27:38,523
He's making 11 layers just like a parfait.

685
00:27:38,590 --> 00:27:41,393
